      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** [Keynesian Cross](note:keynesian-cross): $PE = a + b(Y - T) + I^P + G$; equilibrium where $PE = Y$, $Y^* = (a - bT + I^P + G)/(1 - b)$. Multipliers from [Keynesian Multiplier](note:keynesian-multiplier).\n- **Tests.** Computed in Python (closed form, checked with a root-finder): $Y^* = 1{,}100$; $G = 200 \\to 1{,}600$; $T = 0 \\to 1{,}500$."
      }
